  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Defense obligated $278B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense executed 2,339,613 awards with an average award size of $119K. Obligations fell 43.5% year over year. FY26 totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date results rather than a full year. Yearly obligations before FY26 were $387B in FY21, $414B in FY22, $457B in FY23, $446B in FY24, and $492B in FY25. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest NAICS category at $34.6B, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $26.1B and Engineering Services at $25.2B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice among top vendors with $10.5B and $10.4B, and ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION, RAYTHEON COMPANY, and THE BOEING COMPANY also rank among the largest contractors. The data show concentrated spending in aerospace, weapons systems, engineering, and health-related contracting categories.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large is DoD contracting so far in FY2026?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $278B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense processed 2,339,613 awards with an average award size of $119K. Obligations fell 43.5% year over year, and FY26 totals are partial because they reflect fiscal year to date activity."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Defense spending concentrated?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing leads NAICS categories at $34.6B, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $26.1B and Engineering Services at $25.2B. The Department of Defense also obligated $19.7B to Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences, and $13B to Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers. Vendors concentrate in large aerospace and defense firms, and several health and logistics suppliers appear in the top ten."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Defense spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense obligated $278B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense made 2,339,613 awards with an average award size of $119K, and obligations were down 43.5% year over year, with FY26 totals reported as fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Defense buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense buys aerospace, weapons systems, engineering, R&D, health, and construction services. Aircraft Manufacturing received $34.6B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing received $26.1B, Engineering Services received $25.2B, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences received $19.7B, and Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers received $13B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Defense's largest contractors?",
      "a": "LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION, RAYTHEON COMPANY, and THE BOEING COMPANY are among the largest contractors. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION received $10.5B and $10.4B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION received $8.6B, RAYTHEON COMPANY received $8.1B, and THE BOEING COMPANY received $5.9B and $4.6B."
    }
